"Surah al-Jathiyah begins with the verse, \"The revelation of this Book is from Allah, the Almighty, the All-Wise.\" This emphasizes that the Quran was sent down by Allah and that He is all-conquering and the Possessor of wisdom. Then it is stated that there are numerous signs (proofs) in the heavens and the earth for the believers. These signs point to Allah's existence, might, and power; the believers must examine them and take heed.\n\nIn the creation of man and in the animals, there are also signs for people of assured faith. The creation, diversity, and reproduction of animals demonstrate Allah's power. The alternation of night and day, the sending down of rain to revive the earth, and the directing of the winds are also lessons for a people who understand. These signs point to the Hereafter and the resurrection after death.\n\nWoe to those who hear the verses of Allah and then persist in arrogance! These verses were revealed concerning the likes of Abu Jahl. It is then explained that Allah has subjected the sea to your service so that ships may sail upon it and that you may seek His bounty. Whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth has all been placed at the service of humanity as a grace from Allah; this requires giving thanks.\n\nThe believers are told to forgive those who do not look forward to the days of Allah's retribution. Everyone will be recompensed for what they have earned. The Children of Israel were given the Scripture, judgment, and prophethood; they were provided with wholesome sustenance and favored over the worlds. However, they fell into discord only after knowledge had come to them, out of mutual rivalry. Allah will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection.\n\nProphet Muhammad (peace be upon him) was placed upon a clear path (shariah) in matters of religion; he must follow it and not follow the desires of those who do not know. The wrongdoers are allies of one another, whereas Allah is the Protector of the righteous (al-muttaqun). The Quran is a light, guidance, and mercy for mankind. Do those who commit evil deeds think that they will be treated like those who believe and do righteous deeds? How ill they judge!\n\nAllah created the heavens and the earth in truth; everyone will be recompensed for what they have done, and they will not be wronged. There is no one who can guide the person who takes their own desire as their god, whom Allah has led astray based on His knowledge, and whose hearing and heart He has sealed, and over whose sight He has placed a veil. The polytheists say, \"There is nothing beyond this worldly life of ours; time alone destroys us.\" Yet they have no knowledge of this; they do nothing but conjecture.\n\nWhen the verses are recited to them clearly, the polytheists say, \"Bring back our forefathers if you are truthful.\" Say: \"Allah gives you life, then causes you to die, and then gathers you together on the Day of Resurrection. But most people do not know.\"\n\nTo Allah belongs the dominion of the heavens and the earth. On the Day of Resurrection, those who follow falsehood will be the losers. You will see every community kneeling; each will be summoned to its record. Those who believe and do righteous deeds will enter into mercy; as for the disbelievers, they will be reminded that His verses were recited to them, but they acted arrogantly and denied the Resurrection. The evil of the deeds they committed will become apparent to them, and they will abide in the Fire forever.\n\nPraise be to Allah, Lord of the heavens, Lord of the earth, and Lord of the worlds. All greatness and sovereignty in the heavens and the earth belong to Him. He is the Almighty (all-conquering) and the All-Wise (the Possessor of absolute judgment and wisdom).\n\nThe word 'sa'ah' (the Hour), which refers to the day the Resurrection will occur, is a portion of time according to al-Raghib's explanation. It was given this name by comparison to the Resurrection. Knowledge of when the Resurrection will take place belongs to Allah alone. There are two interpretations of this word: The first is Allah's swift reckoning. The second is that those who witness the Resurrection will think they had remained in the world for only an evening or the morning thereof.\n\nThe concept of the Hour is divided into three categories: The major hour is the resurrection of people for the reckoning. The middle hour is the death of the people of an entire generation. The minor hour is a person's own death. Every individual's death is their personal resurrection. Indeed, it has been said, 'Whoever dies, their resurrection has already come to pass.' However, the Hour mentioned in this verse refers to the general Resurrection.\n\nThe word 'jathiyah' in the verse 'And you will see every community kneeling (jathiyah)' has been interpreted in two ways. The first means kneeling, which expresses respect and a composed posture. The second means a gathered congregation. The intent is the gathering before Allah for the reckoning.\n\nWhat is emphasized in these verses is Allah's absolute sovereignty in the heavens and the earth, the certainty of the Day of Resurrection, and the gathering of all nations before His presence for the reckoning on that day. While explaining these concepts, Elmalılı cited various interpretations, yet did not pass a definitive judgment."